+# Predefined workflows
+
+Implement
+Description: Turn a settled design into a reviewed implementation spec, then implement it.
+Use when: Use when the design is already settled in chat and the work is substantial: multiple dependent phases or architectural decisions whose mistakes would invalidate later phases. Launch only when no user choice or technical uncertainty remains and no phase needs discovery, experiments, or proof-of-concept work; the workflow inspects the repository only to ground the settled design in exact files, callers, and tests. Do not use it to start designing, for a bounded change, for routine ticket-sized work, or for bulk homogeneous work such as mass lint fixes, codemods, or renames. When you can launch a workflow file, run bulk work as one that fans out over the sites and verifies each one; otherwise drive it from chat as waves of implementer subagents with per-batch verification. Once the workflow is running, newly exposed implementation uncertainty belongs to the active step: troubleshoot it, run a focused experiment or proof of concept, and continue. The fact that work remains is not a blocker.
+Path: ${resolve(HANDCRAFTED_WORKFLOW_DIRECTORY, "implement.workflow.yaml")}
+
+QA
+Description: Inventory the user-visible surface, exercise every entry from scratch in each verification pass, fix reproducible issues, and record blocking findings.
+Use when: The user wants an exhaustive QA pass on the current project: "QA the app", "do a full quality pass", "test every surface". Every follow-up pass also exercises the complete surface from scratch. Produces a timestamped run directory under docs/qa/runs/ with a changelog and unclear-findings document, and applies fixes in the same pass.
+Path: ${resolve(HANDCRAFTED_WORKFLOW_DIRECTORY, "qa.workflow.yaml")}
+
+Debug
+Description: Investigate, fix, and verify a small reported issue.
+Use when: Use for a small investigation and fix when the user reports a specific bug and the root cause is not known. The workflow separates root-cause analysis, the fix, and verification. Keep obvious fixes and clear local changes in-process.
+Path: ${resolve(HANDCRAFTED_WORKFLOW_DIRECTORY, "debug.workflow.yaml")}`
+
